Directory: FISSION
File:      actinides_gs_WMM.readme (24 May 2026)
************************************************

                     ACTINIDES_GS_WMM.DAT
Ground-state properties of 75 selected actinide isotopes with Z=89-98
  (Provided by P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, 24 May 2026)
 *****************************************************************

Contents
--------
The file contains ground-state properties calculated using the Warsaw macroscopic-microscopic (WMM) model [1].
It provides ground-state masses, total binding energies, macroscopic and microscopic energy contributions,
and equilibrium deformation parameters for 75 selected actinide nuclei with Z=89-98. All calculations
were performed by minimizing the total energy with respect to seven axially symmetric deformation parameters
that define the nuclear surface in a standard spherical-harmonic expansion. Further details of the model
and computational procedure can be found in Ref. [1].

Format
------
Each record of the file contains

     Z      : proton (charge) number
     N      : neutron number
     A      : mass number
     M      : ground-state mass excess [MeV]
     Etot   : total ground-state energy [MeV]
     Emac   : macroscopic energy contribution [MeV]
     Emic   : microscopic energy contribution [MeV]
     b2-b8  : equilibrium deformation parameters

The corresponding Fortran format specification is (3i4,11f8.2).

References
----------
[1] P. Jachimowicz, M. Kowal, J. Skalski, At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 138, 101393 (2021).
